policy.description:
Complete official firewall policy object. Fetch it with get_firewall_policy;
omitted optional fields are cleared by this PUT.
Advisory spec fields; any JSON passes. Required: action, destination, enabled, ipProtocolScope, loggingEnabled, name, source.

tools.description:
Get a single Dynamic DNS configuration by ID.

Returns: the controller's Classic REST envelope {meta: {rc}, data: [Dynamic DNS entry]}
verbatim. To change it, edit data[0] and pass it as `payload` to update_dynamic_dns.

Returned verbatim, including x_password credential fields (masked when UNIFI_REDACT_SECRETS is enabled).

Example call (get_dynamic_dns):
    {"host": "my-console", "site": "Default", "ddns_id": "000000000000000000000107"}

Get a single WLAN (SSID) configuration by ID.

Returns: the controller's Classic REST envelope {meta: {rc}, data: [WLAN configuration]}
verbatim. To change it, edit data[0] and pass it as `payload` to update_wlan_config.

Returned verbatim, including x_passphrase credential fields (masked when UNIFI_REDACT_SECRETS is enabled).

Example call (get_wlan_config):
    {"host": "my-console", "site": "Default", "wlan_id": "000000000000000000000107"}

query.description:
Legacy free-form object, taking precedence over queries; a {mac, ports}
object is sent as [query]. Shape: {mac:string,ports:integer[]}, e.g.
{"mac": "02:00:5e:00:53:01", "ports": [1, 2]}. Use queries for the UI array.

ports.description:
Ports to clear. Shape: {port_idx:integer,unit_id?:integer}[].
Each item names a port (unit_id for a stack member);
for example [{"port_idx": 5}].

payload.description:
spec: free-form (Network v2 trafficroutes, snake_case). FULL replacement object;
start from get_traffic_route output.
Free-form JSON object; no fixed body shape is published.

types.description:
same filters and validation as `list_protect_events` (camera names resolve to IDs;
smart_detect_types without types is sent with a _warnings entry).
Shape: string|string[]

cameras.description:
same filters and validation as `list_protect_events` (camera names resolve to IDs;
smart_detect_types without types is sent with a _warnings entry).
Shape: string|string[]

key_label.description:
Optional configured API-key label (see list_configured_api_keys) to read one
key. Omit it to cover every key. With several keys configured, page_token needs it;
without it the call fails listing the labels.

threat_types.description:
Optional threat kinds to include, e.g. ["THREAT"] or ["HONEYPOT"];
default ["HONEYPOT", "THREAT"].
Shape: string[]
